From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:20:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 02/33] Router and launch cuts on gfx1100: DPP top-10, router
 tail, GDN a/b ILP, the gfx1100 defaults table, fewer nodes a window

Port of opt7/integrate 4674b8b0 c2999081 74f1bdec 18127ff0 9773eb79 163d880d 1da0aa88 (router, table) and
0a347f12 44b62163 0ef47c13 c3574b6d (launch) onto v0.2.9. One commit: the router tail block in verify.cpp uses the
launch switches' state (the shared gate in the tail, one-token windows), so the two cannot build apart.
- gfx1100 defaults table (STRATA_GFX1100_DEFAULTS=0 turns it off; a switch you set is kept): ROUTE_DPP (top-10 one
  wave per token with DPP), ROUTER_TAIL (router GEMV + top-10 + doorbell in one launch), GDN_AB_ILP (a/b projections
  one warp per row and token, loads first), FUSE_CONVAB, MULTI_BLOCK_ARGMAX. Each bitwise its original.
- Opt-in, set by the run config: SH_GATE_TAIL, COMBINE_MAPPED, QSA_GATE_Q8, MAPPED_FAST, T1_FUSE, QSA_FOLD,
  ROUTER_TAIL_ROWS. QSA_FOLD re-done on v0.2.9's indexer lambdas (idx_key makes the query projection too, main
  stream only; idx_snap skips the tails the window start already took).
- The router tail is not used where something rewrites ids between the top-10 and the ring: v0.2.9's
  STRATA_ROUTE_PRIOR (g_route_prior), ROUTE_RESIDENT, the device plan, the doorbell store, always-publish.
- Dropped STRATA_HEAD_Q8 (not bitwise on HIP, never enabled).
Measured on 0.1.43: router set code +2.7%, edit +1.3%; node cuts 1,674 -> 1,193 nodes a 4-token window, code +5%.
